<title>KYRGYZSTAN: Kyrgyz 3-mth T-bill yield falls to 45.13 percent.</title>
<headline>Kyrgyz 3-mth T-bill yield falls to 45.13 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BISHKEK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of Kyrgyz three-month GKV discount Treasury bills fell to 45.13 at an auction on March 27 from 48.15 at the last auction on March 20, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   March 27	   March 20</p>
<p> Series number			 13/3		 12/3</p>
<p> Issue volume (million som)	    5.00		 5.00</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million som)	   18.19		17.03</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million som)	   5.00		 5.00</p>
<p> Average price			 89.76 pct	  89.15</p>
<p> Lowest accepted price	     89.73		89.15</p>
<p> Average yield			 45.13		48.15</p>
<p> Highest accepted yield	    45.28		48.15</p>
<p> Tenor (remaining)		   91 days	   91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				June 30, 1997   June 23, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
